# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5; L §5.19 Readings at a place that keeps parts). L §5.19 Stated parts against booked parts: "a stated part is q's balance ... Where it differs from q's booked part,
# the difference is q's own gap: where positive, a part of q's of that amount ...; where negative, a take of q's parts by
# the leaving rule, its terms on w holes as above. The unstated rest has a gap of its own, over the labels the reading
# doesn't state, by the anchor's rules above".
# At a place both owned and batched, tomek's stated 50.00 over his booked 0.00 is "a part of q's of that amount": his,
# its batch open (L §8.1: "only a gap or a merge across batches leaves its batch open"), so tomek's balance is known and
# a1's (or (tomek, a1)'s) is HOLE-PART; the unstated rest is ania's 100.00 as booked (scratch/exp7.py). The question's
# text is refcore's.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of a1, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of (tomek, a1)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 150.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
  stated[konto] of tomek = 50.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
=== expect
q: (150.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, ?"konto: 50.00 PLN may be a1's: which batches are tomek's 50.00 PLN of konto at 2026-03-31 end?" (konto), ?"konto: 50.00 PLN may be (tomek, a1)'s: which batches are tomek's 50.00 PLN of konto at 2026-03-31 end?" (konto))
  anchor: konto 2026-03-31 end, stated 150.00 PLN, difference 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-01
